<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="49d33314-23db-5e9c-841b-320ecdcd98f4" activityNameId="18468a64-2b24-52d8-9959-60086ed1bbaa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, average train</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, average train
The operation, demand and maintanance of the train has been allocated based on the yearly train kilometric performance 37489 Mio pkm. The demand of rail track has been allocated based on the demand of infrastructure per gross tonne kilometric performance in Switzerland 3.3E-8 km/gtkm. The losses at the overhead line (7%) are assumed to be higher than the losses in CH (5.03%)\nTechnology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional gravel track beddings. For the manufacturing of vehicles, the data reflects the currently dominating train type (IC2000) of Switzerland.\nTime period: Time of publications\nVersion: 1\nEnergy values: Undefined\n100.0\nProduction volume: Unknown\nLocal category: Transportsysteme\nLocal subcategory: Schiene\nUVEK 2022 source file:713_Transport-Train-passenger-average_RER&amp;CH_EIV2_v0.3._X-Transport Train RER.xml\n\n
UUID: 12b88b32-2331-388d-a693-adb5a7933ab2
The module calls the modules  "production and maintenance of vehicles"; "construction and maintenance of railway tracks". The module includes the operation (energy consumption and emissione) of the train.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional gravel track beddings. For the manufacturing of vehicles, the data reflects the currently dominating train type (IC2000) of Switzerland.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_12b88b32-2331-388d-a693-adb5a7933ab2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
